# Relinking mongoose @VERSION@ with a modified libnfs

This kit is the machine-readable work/source material for the mongoose
@VERSION@ executable that statically includes libnfs. It is intentionally
self-contained for Rust dependencies and can be built with Cargo offline.

## Exact release inputs

- mongoose revision: `@MONGOOSE_SHA@`
- libnfs repository: <@LIBNFS_URL@>
- libnfs revision: `@LIBNFS_SHA@`
- official `libnfs.a` SHA-256: `@LIBNFS_STATIC_SHA@`
- nfs-walker repository: <@NFS_WALKER_URL@>
- nfs-walker revision: `@NFS_WALKER_SHA@`
- target: `x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu.2.34`
- Rust: `@RUSTC_VERSION@`
- Cargo: `@CARGO_VERSION@`
- cargo-zigbuild: `@CARGO_ZIGBUILD_VERSION@`
- Zig: `@ZIG_VERSION@`
- CMake: `@CMAKE_VERSION@`
- GNU ar/ranlib: `@BINUTILS_VERSION@`

The official archive was built by `build-libnfs-static.sh`; its path-remapping
flags make an unmodified `libnfs.a` reproducible across checkout directories.
The mongoose release profile uses LTO, one codegen unit, `panic=abort`, and
stripping, as recorded in `mongoose/Cargo.toml`.

## Build a replacement

Install the toolchain versions above, set `ZIG` to the Zig executable if it is
not on `PATH`, and make any interface-compatible changes under `libnfs/`.
Then, from the extracted kit root:

```sh
./build-libnfs-static.sh --source ./libnfs --output ./modified-stage

cd mongoose
export VAMOOSE_LIBNFS_DIR="$PWD/../modified-stage"
export NFS_WALKER_LIBNFS_DIR="$PWD/../modified-stage"
export CARGO_ZIGBUILD_ZIG_PATH="${ZIG:-zig}"
cargo zigbuild --release --locked --offline \
  --target x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu.2.34 -p mongoose
```

The replacement executable is
`mongoose/target/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/release/mongoose`. Both mongoose
libnfs consumers explicitly link the replacement static archive from the two
environment variables above.

## Automated proof

`verify-relink.sh` copies the bundled libnfs source, makes a harmless but
binary-visible change to an out-of-memory diagnostic, builds it, runs the
mongoose library smoke tests against it, produces a portable replacement
binary, verifies that the marker reached that binary, and confirms there is no
dynamic libnfs dependency:

```sh
./verify-relink.sh --original /path/to/mongoose-linux-x86_64 \
  --evidence ./RELINK-VERIFICATION.txt
```

The release's successful run is recorded in the companion
`RELINK-VERIFICATION.txt` asset. This procedure does not require or permit
network access; all Cargo dependencies are in `mongoose/vendor/`.
